# Investing documentation conventions

When creating or editing specs under `investing/docs/`:

## Feature specs

Follow the structure used in existing features (e.g. `investing/docs/features/cheap-stocks.md`):

- Objective
- MVP scope / Out of MVP scope
- Inputs (tables where helpful)
- Flow or logic (include at least one **Mermaid** diagram when the flow changes)
- Acceptance criteria
- Risks

Add **Implementation status** when coding starts: `planned` | `in_progress` | `done`.

## Architecture spec

- Record closed decisions in tables (see "Decisions made so far" in `investing/docs/architecture/architecture.md`).
- Cross-link feature files from the module table.
- Do not contradict a closed architecture decision without updating the architecture doc first.

## Cross-links

Link related feature specs and point to shared definitions (e.g. shared `EBIT` between quality and cheapness modules).

## Language

All spec text must be in English.
